Input: {"question": "What channel is NewsChannel 5 affiliated with?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 0, "end": 195, "text": "KRGV-TV KRGV-TV, virtual channel 5 (VHF digital channel 13), is an ABC-affiliated television station licensed to Weslaco, Texas, United States and serving the Rio Grande Valley metropolitan area."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 196, "end": 348, "text": "The station is owned by the Manship family of Baton Rouge, Louisiana through Mobile Video Tapes, Inc., which often does business as KRGV-TV Corporation."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 349, "end": 472, "text": "KRGV's studios are located on East Expressway (I-2/US 83) in Weslaco, and its transmitter is located in Santa Maria, Texas."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 473, "end": 537, "text": "On cable, the station can be seen on Charter Spectrum channel 5."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 538, "end": 602, "text": "KRGV is also available on channel 5 on DirecTV and Dish Network."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "start": 603, "end": 619, "text": "KRGV joined as a"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "the first digital television station on the air in the Rio Grande Valley ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 75, "end": 161, "text": "This new technology featured high definition ( HD ) programming from the ABC Network ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 162, "end": 272, "text": "A few months later , KRGV-DT added digital channel 5.2 displaying local weather information around the clock ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 273, "end": 406, "text": "In May of 2007 , LATV was introduced on 5.2 , providing music and entertainment programming oriented to the young Hispanic audience ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 407, "end": 467, "text": "December 2008 marked the launch of Retro TV on channel 5.3 ."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d01", "start": 468, "end": 573, "text": "This network brought back many of the favorite programs from the early years of television , available 24"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 0, "end": 163, "text": "WPTV-TV WPTV-TV is an NBC-affiliated television station licensed to West Palm Beach, Florida, United States, serving the Gold and Treasure Coasts of South Florida."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 164, "end": 312, "text": "It broadcasts a high definition digital signal on VHF channel 12 (or virtual channel 5 via PSIP) from a transmitter in Lake Worth along US 441/SR 7."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 313, "end": 343, "text": "The station is owned by the E."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 344, "end": 346, "text": "W."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 347, "end": 474, "text": "Scripps Company, which also operates Fox affiliate WFLX (channel 29) under a shared services agreement with owner Raycom Media."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "start": 475, "end": 614, "text": "The two stations share studios on South Australian Avenue in downtown West Palm Beach (mailing address says Banyan Boulevard, also known as"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": ".3 Health Ch ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03", "start": 15, "end": 243, "text": ".4 PBS Kids WFOR-TV 4 .1 CBS .2 Start .3 Dabl .4 Fave .5 Catchy WTVJ 6 .1 NBC .2 Cozi .3 AmCrimes .4 Oxygen WSVN 7 .1 Fox .2 365BLK → ABC .3 Defy WGEN-TV 8 .1 Estrella TV .2/.4 LC .3 HQ .5 Nosey .6 Confess WPLG 10 .1 ABC → Ind ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03", "start": 244, "end": 286, "text": ".2 MeTV .3 H & I WURH-CD 13 .1 Health Ch ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03", "start": 287, "end": 412, "text": "WLRN-TV 17 .1 PBS WSBS-TV 22 .1 Mega TV .2 CLAFE WLTV-DT 23 .1 UNI .2 Crime .3 Mystery .5 NV .6 LC WBFS-TV 33 .1 CW .2 Movies"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 0, "end": 80, "text": "Cleveland television station to begin broadcasting newscasts in high-definition."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 81, "end": 208, "text": "At present, all locally produced portions of the station's newscasts, including live remote field footage, are presented in HD."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 209, "end": 341, "text": "It was also around this time that channel 5 introduced the modified version of the classic \"Circle 5\" logo that was used until 2016."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 342, "end": 400, "text": "Sister station WPTV also uses the classic \"Circle 5\" logo."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 401, "end": 513, "text": "On May 21, 2009, Ted Henry retired as the primary news anchor at channel 5, after holding the post for 33 years."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 514, "end": 587, "text": "Henry is the longest serving news anchor in Cleveland television history."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d04", "start": 588, "end": 617, "text": "In November 2010, WEWS became"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d05", "start": 0, "end": 98, "text": "and Order in favor of two UHF allocations , one of which was not considered operable at the time ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d05", "start": 99, "end": 272, "text": "[ 21 ] The station largely lost money in its early years and relied on profits from WAKR to remain solvent [ 22 ] even after it moved from channel 49 to channel 23 in 1967 ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d05", "start": 273, "end": 506, "text": "[ 23 ] The ABC-TV schedule began to be carried in pattern by WAKR-TV with minimal deviations starting with the 1963–64 television season [ 24 ] and carried Good Morning America in its entirety for the market as WEWS opted out for The"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d00:c0", "entity": "NewsChannel 5", "scope": "affiliation", "claim": "NewsChannel 5 is affiliated with ABC.", "answer": "ABC", "quote": "KRGV-TV KRGV-TV, virtual channel 5 (VHF digital channel 13), is an ABC-affiliated television station licensed to Weslaco, Texas, United States and serving the Rio Grande Valley metropolitan area.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d02:c0", "entity": "NewsChannel 5", "scope": "affiliation", "claim": "NewsChannel 5 is affiliated with NBC.", "answer": "NBC", "quote": "WPTV-TV WPTV-TV is an NBC-affiliated television station licensed to West Palm Beach, Florida, United States, serving the Gold and Treasure Coasts of South Florida.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0396-8dc82e76946c:d03:c0", "entity":